WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.371
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.371 --> 00:00:02.204
- All right y'all.

00:00:02.204 --> 00:00:03.150
We always like to end the show

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:04.710
with something you can feel good about.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.947
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.947 --> 00:00:09.070
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.025
We've talked a lot here,
about little things

00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:13.500
we can do to help save
this planet of ours.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.145
And often there are small actions

00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:17.830
that don't just protect the earth,

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.640
they actually can help people
living on it right now.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.400
And LA Mama is proving
it with her organization,

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.300
Crayon Collection, people donate unused

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.393
or gently used crayons

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.673
keeping them out of
landfills, which is amazing.

00:00:29.673 --> 00:00:32.230
Then they make their way to kids

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.000
who otherwise wouldn't have them.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.170
It's pretty smart, right? And
that's just the beginning.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.290
We have this mama of action
on the line right now.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.377
Everybody say hi to Sheila who watches

00:00:40.377 --> 00:00:44.336
on NBC for Los Angeles. Hi Sheila.

00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:45.350
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.060
Thanks so much for having me today.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.440
- Absolutely. Well, tell us more about

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.800
the Crayon Collection.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.360
- The Crayon Collection is my
organization that I started

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.650
with my little toddler
daughter when she was

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.620
a super picky eater and we
kept going to restaurants.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.550
She'd get a free four
pack of crayons each time

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.990
and sometimes she wouldn't
even use the crayons

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.750
but they'd still end up in the
trash at the end of the meal.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.140
And this really drove me crazy

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.950
coz I knew so many kids need them

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:13.196
and the planet cannot take any
more trash in our landfills.

00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:15.570
When I found out crayons
are thrown away at a

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.300
rate of 150 million per year
from restaurants in America,

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.383
I had to do something.

00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:21.216
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:21.216 --> 00:01:22.970
- So I started asking grass
restaurants to collect

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.220
the crayons kids leave
behind and I would find

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.190
a local school that was super vulnerable

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.720
also known as Title 1
schools to benefit from them.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.710
Later on, we would go inside the classroom

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.470
with professional artists
with our art education program

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:38.480
and teach our really cool
art projects to reinsert that

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.130
into schools and it makes a huge impact.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.820
We've done this for a while,

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:46.222
so we've donated over 22
million crayons to date.

00:01:46.222 --> 00:01:47.055
- Wow.

00:01:47.055 --> 00:01:50.270
- We have had hundred
thousand kids served.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.370
We're in all 50 states, 10 countries.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.180
And we even set a Guinness World Record

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.600
where we donated 1 million, 9,500 crayons

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.453
to over 900 teachers right
here in LA in one day.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.150
(audience applauding)

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.211
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:03.211 --> 00:02:05.740
It's an amazing thing coz
everything is being helped.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.580
The planets being helped, the
landfills are being helped.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.413
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:08.413 --> 00:02:09.246
The kids are being helped.

00:02:09.246 --> 00:02:10.630
Everyone kind of wins in this scenario.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.240
It's a beautiful thing
that you've created.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.360
I love also that it's not

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.410
about putting even more of a
carbon footprint out there.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:16.630
You're actually like going local

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.690
like help the people that
live in your community.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.770
That's so cool.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.150
Thank you so much, Sheila.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.200
I'm Liking your posts right now. Okay.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.540
- [Sheila] Thank you so so much.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.870
- Absolutely. And that's not all.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.410
Our season long partner
Pilot Pen makers of Frixion,

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.980
the go to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.100
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.700
just like you ma'am, so
they're gonna give you

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.130
a thousand dollars to help out.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.087
How's that sound?
(audience cheering)

00:02:37.087 --> 00:02:39.647
- Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:02:39.647 --> 00:02:41.967
- [Kelly] Absolutely
have a good one Sheila.

